# Files that must never be propagated from this repository to other Cratis repositories.
# Patterns work like .gitignore; unscoped patterns are relative to .github/.
# See Cratis/Workflows README, "Excluding files from synchronization".

# Project-local instructions. PROJECT.md is the one file that describes only THIS repository —
# its issue tracker, endpoints, credentials, deployment recipes, and the conventions that
# override the shared corpus here. Syncing it means the last repository to publish overwrites
# every other repository's project-local context.
#
# This entry is THE ONLY DEFENSE THIS REPOSITORY HAS, and it protects only this repository.
# .copilot-sync-ignore is read from the SOURCE repository of a propagation run, so this entry
# stops this repository from broadcasting its PROJECT.md and does nothing to stop another
# repository broadcasting its copy into this one.
#
# An earlier version of this comment claimed the real guard was an unconditional
# .agents/PROJECT.md exclusion in prepare-copilot-source-artifact.sh in Cratis/Workflows.
# THAT GUARD DOES NOT EXIST. That script selects .agents wholesale --- the path regex is
# `^(AGENTS\.md$|\.agents(/|$)|...)` --- and the only path it hardcodes an exclusion for is
# .claude/settings.local.json. Every repository that is a propagation source and has no
# .copilot-sync-ignore of its own will broadcast its PROJECT.md to every other repository.
#
# This has already happened, and it is not hypothetical: on 2026-07-30 Cratis/Chronicle
# broadcast its PROJECT.md into Automation, Narrator, Prompter, Specifications and
# VerticalSlices, where a file titled "Chronicle --- Project-Specific Instructions" is still
# served today as those repositories' own project-local instructions. Cratis/Lens was
# repaired by hand afterwards ("Restore Lens project-local instructions"). Because AGENTS.md
# gives .agents/PROJECT.md authority OVER the shared corpus for its repository, a foreign
# copy does not merely add noise --- it outranks the corpus with another repository's rules.
#
# The durable fix belongs in Cratis/Workflows, which this repository must not modify: exclude
# .agents/PROJECT.md in prepare-copilot-source-artifact.sh so no source can broadcast it,
# regardless of whether that source remembered to write this file.
.agents/PROJECT.md
